<Footnotes>
  <li>React Native and Expo, not native. One engineer cannot maintain two codebases at one-release-per-week cadence. EAS Update lets me push JS fixes between App Store reviews, which is how 68 releases in a year is even possible.</li>
  <li>The shortcut that still bills me interest: the community's feed ranking started as a single Postgres query with a hand-tuned score. It scaled past where I expected, then started showing its age. Shipping it in two weeks was right. Living with the query for a year was the tax.</li>
</Footnotes>
